{
  "analysis": "Full config reviewed. Key edits needed: line 8 enable CPU_ONLY, line 50 set BLAS to openblas. No WITH_HDF5 option in this version (HDF5 auto-detected). Python layer stays disabled. Two big risks for building old Caffe 1.0.0 (2016 code) on Ubuntu 24.04: (1) protobuf 3.x vs the 2.6 API Caffe was written against, (2) BLAS library naming. Let me check protobuf version, BLAS libs, python3 version, and how the Makefile resolves BLAS before editing and building.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /app/caffe && echo '=== protobuf ===' && protoc --version && dpkg -l 2>/dev/null | grep -iE 'protobuf' | awk '{print $2,$3}'; echo '=== BLAS libs ===' && ls /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/ | grep -iE 'blas|lapack|cblas'; echo '=== python3 ===' && python3 --version && ls /usr/include/python3.12 2>/dev/null | head -1; echo '=== Makefile BLAS handling ===' && grep -nE 'BLAS|atlas|openblas' Makefile | head -n 40\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}
